  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0}\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\left[\\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{x+1}{2 x+1}\\right)-\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right]$\n$=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0}\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\left[\\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{x+1}{2 x+1}\\right)-\\tan ^{-1}(1)\\right]$\n$=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0}\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right) \\cdot \\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\frac{x+1}{2 x+1}-1}{1+\\frac{x+1}{2 x+1}}\\right)$\n$=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{1}{x} \\cdot \\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{-x}{3 x+2}\\right)$\n$=-\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0}\\left[\\frac{\\tan ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{x}{3 x+2}\\right)}{\\frac{x}{3 x+2}} \\times \\frac{1}{3 x+2}\\right]=-\\frac{1}{2}$",
    "image": null
  },
